id=derp_memtune
name=Derp memory tuning (LMK + sysctl, persisted)
version=v1
versionCode=10001
author=Derp
description=Makes the memory tuning measured in docs/15-MEMORY-MANAGEMENT.md §22/#24 durable across reboot. Until now it was applied by hand with hm_mod/memtune_apply.sh and lived only until the next boot, which silently returned the device to the kill-storm behaviour (0->140 kills in ~5 s, MemFree floor 46-67 MB, camera process dead at +12-16 s). This module re-applies the validated table at late_start, AFTER lmkd has written its own default table, because lmkd rewrites /sys/module/lowmemorykiller/parameters/minfree on every boot and an earlier write is simply overwritten. The applied set is exactly the one measured live: minfree 12288,16384,20480,24576,61440,81920 (adj-0 tier down 72->48 MB so camera/provider leave the kill set except as a last resort; cached tiers up 216/315 -> 240/320 MB so cached apps die earlier in the climb), extra_free_kbytes 13162->24576, vfs_cache_pressure 50->150, page-cluster 0->3, zswap max_pool_percent 20->25. Kernel #214's lmk-bp (kill pacing via task_lmk_waiting / kill_interval_ms=100) is what turned that into "kills +0 for 32 s+", MemFree floor 68-80 MB, and the camera process alive minutes later, so this tuning is only claimed as the complement to that build, not a substitute. Kept as a SEPARATE module from derp_raw12_t1 on purpose: the camera HAL payload is rebuilt and swapped every bisect rung, and the memory tuning must survive those swaps. Nothing here restarts the camera provider, and uninstall.sh restores the stock table.
patch_extra=Trap that shaped this module (docs/15 §22.2): writing the minfree parameter with SPACE-separated values zeroed the array, the driver's array_size collapsed to 0, and the in-kernel LMK was silently disabled leaving only the OOM killer. The write therefore uses commas and service.sh verifies the readback; if the table does not read back exactly, the stock table is restored immediately and the failure is logged. page-cluster=3 is applied for fidelity with the measured set but is inert on this build (CONFIG_SWAP_ENABLE_READAHEAD is unset, docs/15 §21.1). extra_free_kbytes is capped at 24576 to keep the kswapd band at 32+24 = 56 MB, matching the research cap of ~64 MB total.
